index 71efa04..3136025 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -28,6 +28,8 @@ The UI uses the original SnowPakTool cache-block and PAK writer classes and writ
 
 Map truck replacements are queued in the popup and written from **Start → Map files**. The map writer updates both scene size boundaries, preserves the PAK entry order and each entry's compression method, and copies unrelated ZIP records unchanged. Original maps and previous edited versions remain backed up under `workspace/region-maps/backups`. **Repair saved maps** rebuilds outputs produced by the older writer using their original archive layout, while retaining the selected trucks. Repair verifies the unchanged scene payload and unrelated archive contents before replacing a workspace output; it never writes installed game files. Reload and review any pending replacements after repairing their source map.
 
+Regions-Trucks uses `workspace/region-maps/backups/<map>/original.pak` (or `original.bin`) as the baseline whenever present. Saved workspace maps override that baseline and pending replacements override the displayed rows. Deleting an updated map therefore restores the backed-up placements on reload or when returning to the tab. Maps without a workspace backup are read from the selected map folder. Workspace backups and updates can also be used without the installed map folder.
